------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web GeofenceDrawer.tsx -> native), no scope narrowing
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • Data: web `useMap()` is react-leaflet's parent-map handle (NOT an HTTP hook) — the
    component is a passive draw controller over the map's persisted `fences`. Native binds
    those fences + the allowed modes + the map focus + freshness through the P1/S8
    GeofenceDrawerSource seam (production wraps the shared map holder); no HTTP in the view.
  • Render decision: web `fenceToLayer` (circle when lat/lng/radius present AND radius>0;
    polygon when ring>=3; else nothing) -> GeofenceGeometry.renderKind, incl. circle-wins-
    when-both, unit-asserted.
  • Geometry: web `layerToGeometry` circle/rectangle/polygon ported; the rectangle bounds ->
    4-corner ring [sw,(ne.lat,sw.lng),ne,(sw.lat,ne.lng)] pinned verbatim by a test; corners
    normalised to sw/ne (getSouthWest/getNorthEast).
  • describeFence: "{name} — {radius.toFixed(0)}m circle around {lat.toFixed(4)},
    {lng.toFixed(4)}" / "{name} — {N}-vertex polygon" / name; default name "Geofence";
    locale-independent toFixed (en_US_POSIX). The web's only user-facing prose is promoted
    to P1/S10 keys. NB the circle branch guards on radius PRESENCE (not >0) — distinct from
    renderKind — pinned by testCircleDescriptionUsesPresenceNotPositiveRadius.
  • Draw modes: web `GeofenceMode` ('circle'|'polygon'|'rectangle', default ['circle'])
    reproduced; the leaflet-draw click/edit/delete handlers become the GeofenceDraft reducer
    (tap -> point, slider -> radius, commit -> NewGeofence) + the model onCreate/onEdit/
    onDelete seam.
  • Leaf-state widening: the web controller renders no loading/empty/error of its own; the
    Apple modal-surface contract adds them (loading / friendly empty / retryable error) PLUS
    the stale+offline freshness axis. The map + toolbar stay LIVE through the empty + content
    phases so the first fence is always drawable (documented enhancement, NOT silent drift).
  • Charts/maps: web Leaflet -> MapKit (Map / MapCircle / MapPolygon / MapPolyline /
    MapReader); NO Recharts in the source, so no Swift Charts.
  • Tailwind classes were NOT ported; chrome is P1/S9 tokens (TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS/
    Font.TS) via the shared TSGlassPanel / TSFadeIn / TSButton.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STATES (every state renders — no hidden surfaces)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  loading  -> GeofenceLoadingState (spinner + "Loading geofences…").
  empty    -> GeofenceEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView "No geofences yet" + hint) beneath
              a LIVE map + toolbar, so the first fence is drawable.
  error    -> GeofenceErrorState (panel + Retry -> model.refresh()), never a blank box.
  stale    -> freshness chip "Stale" + connectivity banner + ONE guarded auto-refresh.
  offline  -> freshness chip "Offline" + banner; cached snapshot kept; no refetch.
  content  -> live map + draw toolbar + saved-fences list (+ inline reload error if a refresh
              failed while a cached snapshot remains).
  Telemetry: model.start() emits P1/S11 view.opened surface="GeofenceDrawer" (once,
  idempotent — ModelTests proven).

